# Folio Health — copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# Both values are read SERVER-SIDE only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix). The browser
# never talks to Medplum directly: it calls this app's /api/fhir/* routes, which
# attach the access token from an httpOnly cookie. That keeps FHIR tokens out of
# browser JavaScript and means the Medplum server's CORS allowlist does not need
# to include this app's origin.

# Base URL of the Medplum server, with a trailing slash.
#   Self-hosted:    http://localhost:8103/
#   Medplum cloud:  https://api.medplum.com/
#
# WARNING: if this is a plain http:// URL over a public network, credentials and
# patient data travel unencrypted. Put TLS in front of the server before it
# holds real patient data.
MEDPLUM_BASE_URL=

# Public ClientApplication id from your Medplum project.
# This is an identifier, not a secret — but it is environment-specific, so it
# stays out of source control.
MEDPLUM_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Service account (first-login password changes) ───────────────────────────
#
# Used for exactly ONE privileged action: clearing a user's `temp-credential`
# flag after they set a permanent password. Everything else in this app acts
# with the signed-in user's own token.
#
# Why it is needed: Medplum revokes every Login on /auth/changepassword, and the
# login created by the re-login that follows is refused Bot/$execute. So the
# user's own session provably cannot clear its own flag. Without an actor
# independent of that session, anyone who sets a permanent password is asked to
# set another one on every sign-in, forever.
#
# To create it, as a PROJECT ADMIN of your Medplum project:
#   POST admin/projects/<projectId>/client  { "name": "Folio Credential Service" }
# which returns the id and a generated secret. The Medplum admin console does the
# same thing under Project settings → Clients → New ClientApplication.
#
# It needs NO AccessPolicy and NO admin membership: a ClientApplication created
# this way can already read and update Practitioner within its own project, which
# is the only thing this credential does (verified against Medplum 5.1.17 — the
# flag-stripping PUT returns 200). Do not grant it more than it needs.
#
# It is NOT the super-admin bootstrap client. That one exists to create projects
# and admin clients across tenants; this one only edits one field on one
# Practitioner, and a project admin can mint it without super-admin rights.
#
# THIS IS A REAL SECRET. It is server-side only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix) and
# must never be committed or exposed to the browser.
#
# Leaving these blank is safe: the app still runs and still forces the password
# change, but cannot auto-clear the flag — /api/auth/change-password will say so
# rather than leaving the user in a silent loop.
MEDPLUM_SERVICE_CLIENT_ID=
MEDPLUM_SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET=
